The listing of courses expires by itself (\cref{sec:course-listing-outage}), and
a course you were added to used to stay invisible until the cache was cleared by
hand.
Let's verify this through the real encrypted round trip, since what failed was
the behaviour of a cache restored from disk.
The HTTP layer is stubbed with [[responses]] because Canvas's answer must change
between the run that wrote the cache and the one that reads it, which a recording
cannot express.

