\subsection{Kinds the user keeps out of the file}
\label{sec:cache-exclude-in-file}

The third filter leaves out the kinds of objects that the user has named, such
as users and submissions, for those who don't want student data on disk
(\cref{sec:cache-exclude}).
The filter needs one thing from this module that the other two do not.

They make the file smaller, and it does not matter when: the next save will
do.
An exclusion is a promise about what is on disk, and the next save may be far
away, since a command that sends no request does not save
(\cref{sec:skip-unchanged-save}).
Someone who turns the exclusion on and then only reads pages from the cache
would keep every roster in the file.
So the file says what it excludes, in the envelope next to the version, and a
save is not skipped while a kind is excluded that the file does not say it
excludes.
That save happens once: afterwards the file says so.

The record is in the envelope and not in the [[Canvas]] object, like the
version, because it describes the file.
A copy of this library that does not know the key reads only the version and
the object, as before.
What such a copy saves has no record, and may hold the excluded kinds again if
that program fetched them, so our next run saves once more.
An exclusion holds for the file only if every program that writes it excludes
the same.

As with the request count, we remember for each [[Canvas]] object what the
file excluded when the object last matched it.
<<functions>>=
def excluded_kinds():
  """Return the kinds of objects to leave out of the cache file."""
  return canvaslms.hacks.canvasapi.CACHE_EXCLUDE

def remember_excluded(canvas, kinds):
  """Note that the cache file of `canvas` excludes `kinds`."""
  try:
    excluded_in_file[canvas] = frozenset(kinds)
  except TypeError:
    pass

def not_yet_excluded(canvas):
  """Return the excluded kinds that the cache file of `canvas` may still hold."""
  try:
    return excluded_kinds() - excluded_in_file.get(canvas, frozenset())
  except TypeError:
    return excluded_kinds()
<<constants>>=
excluded_in_file = weakref.WeakKeyDictionary()
